# Line endings.
#
# This repo gets worked on from more than one machine, including a WSL
# checkout living on a Windows/OneDrive path, where something along the
# way rewrites files with CRLF. Without a rule, every such round trip
# showed a dozen files as "modified" with the entire contents replaced by
# identical contents — burying real changes and making a diff useless for
# reviewing anything.
#
# text=auto lets git decide what's text; eol=lf pins what lands in the
# working tree, on every platform. LF everywhere is the right choice here
# because everything this repo produces is run on Linux: Go sources, shell
# scripts, and a terminal multiplexer whose whole job is talking to a pty.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The recorded demo, and anything like it: never touched, never diffed as
# text.
*.gif binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
